# Quectel modems (VID 2c7c): make sure the USB network function comes up as ECM
# (AT+QCFG="usbnet",1) and not RNDIS, which we have no host driver for.
#
# Matched on the parent USB device so it fires once per plug-in instead of once
# per serial interface. The switch itself runs as a systemd oneshot, because the
# modem has to be reset afterwards and udev must not be blocked that long.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="2c7c", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="quectel-ecm.service"

# The DHCP client for the ECM net device is deliberately *not* started from here.
# There used to be a second rule:
#
#   SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2c7c", \
#     TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="quectel-ecm-up.service"
#
# and it never worked on this board, because 79-quectel-ecm-name.rules renames the
# interface: the rename produces a second uevent with ACTION=move, the rule does
# not match it, and the udev database entry is rewritten without SYSTEMD_WANTS. So
# wwan0 came up only after a manual "systemctl start quectel-ecm-up.service".
# quectel-ecm-up.service is now WantedBy= the wwan0 device unit instead, which is
# level-triggered and needs no property to survive. See that unit for the evidence.
#
# The mode switch above stays on udev because there is no device unit for "a
# Quectel appeared on USB" to hang it off.
